! mcp_bootstrap_p133.strap -- the MCP PROGRAM-ERROR / MASKABLE-
! INTERRUPT exits, printed page 133.  docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF
! p.140, header READ and not assumed: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID
! 11D11MCP   CARD ID ED000101   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER
! 133", and the header's own "LOCATION 216500" names the page's
! first word.
!
! FIFTY-ONE LINES.  The card-serial column runs ED000101 (line 1) to
! ED000151 (line 51), fifty-one consecutive serials for fifty-one
! lines, ONE CARD PER LINE.  Counted off the serial column, nothing
! fell off the top or the bottom of the render.
!
! >>> THE VOLUME SURVEY SAW A WINDOW, NOT THE PAGE. <<<
! docs/mcp_page_map.json scores this page "34 rows, 216501.00 ..
! 216551.4C".  The page has 51 rows running 216500.40 .. 216563.70.
! The survey's LOCATION-column OCR stops at its own line 42 and it
! drops the rows whose location it cannot read; the serial column
! above is what makes 51 a reading rather than a guess.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN IS READ, AND IT IS ASSERTED, NOT CHECKED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE PAGE PRINTS NO SLC. <<<  216500.40 is line 1's own
! LOCATION; the header's "LOCATION 216500" prints the word.  So the
! "SLC,(8)216500.40" below is a READING of line 1, not a test of
! contiguity with printed p.132 -- a hard SLC overrides the arriving
! counter silently (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "A HARD SLC
! CANNOT DISAGREE WITH THE ARRIVING COUNTER").  pp.129-132 are not
! transcribed.  The volume OCR of printed p.132 (PDF p.139) carries
! a row at 216500.00 as its last readable line, which is consistent
! with a clean join to 216500.40, but p.132 may have lines below
! that the OCR dropped, so the join is NOT confirmed here.  When
! p.132 lands, compare by hand.
!
! >>> "!SYM YMCPPE 216500.40" IS NOT A CHECK. <<<  It is the SLC
! target, so it passes by construction.  Every OTHER !SYM below is a
! real check, because the counter has to walk to it.
!
! THE FORWARD JOIN HAS A WITNESS AND IT AGREES.  Line 51 is an
! (AX)DD entry whose datum is ten blanks, so the counter leaves it
! at 216565.10; the volume OCR of printed p.134 (PDF p.141) reads
! its line 1 as "216565.40 000000.30 00 CNOP".  A CNOP advances to
! the next HALF WORD, 216565.10 -> 216565.40, exactly.  See "CNOP
! ALIGNMENT" below -- the same rule is witnessed a second time
! INSIDE this page at lines 13/14.
!
! TAIL SCOPE.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the
! origin and pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the TAIL,(2)G block that printed p.2
! opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed with UNTAIL,(2).  YUXSAV
! below is the clearest case: printed pp.38/40/41 define a YUXSAV at
! 002324.00 and this page's YUXSAV is 231363.00.  That is tail
! scope, NOT a collision; it is recorded, not "fixed".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE CONTAINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 1-11   YMCPPE, the MCP program-error exit.  It loads the
!              console channel (SYCOCH), releases both channels,
!              turns the console lights on through YMFCF+1, copies
!              the saved index registers out of YUXSAV, writes the
!              YMCPCW control-word chain to the console and halts on
!              itself at YMCPHP ("BD,YMCPHP" is a branch-disabled
!              loop on its own address).  Lines 10-11 are the two
!              I/O CONTROL WORDS that chain: YMCPC2 writes the
!              7-byte YMCPCM code and YMCPCW writes 3 words of
!              YMFCF, chaining to YMCPC2.
! Lines 12-17  the message area: YPPEM / YPEIC (mode A, the 48
!              character set) and YMCPCM / YMCPIN (mode IQS, the
!              console typewriter set).  Line 14 is the CNOP that
!              realigns after line 13's odd-length datum.
! Lines 18-19  YFXTS and YEXEFX, two "B,WRAM" slots.  printed p.114
!              already references both, at 216530.00 and 216530.40,
!              and its deck SYNs them there -- a landed second
!              reading of two of this page's own symbols.
! Lines 20-48  YMSF, the maskable-interrupt exit.  It transmits the
!              30 words of S T LR / SLRBU, loads the interrupted
!              address, converts the saved IC to BCD into YMIMIN,
!              decrements the maskable-interrupt count YMISCO and
!              either writes the spool message (SIC/B calling
!              sequence at lines 42-45, whose two parameter words
!              are YMIMIN and the count 8) or, when the count has
!              not run out, branches to YTMMI -> STMMI -> S DISP.
! Lines 49-51  YMIMIN and YMIMIC, the message the spooler prints.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! CNOP ALIGNMENT, WITNESSED TWICE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! An entry-mode DD compiles EIGHT BITS PER CHARACTER with the
! end-of-statement character not compiled (strap/charsets.py).  Two
! rows on this page land the counter on a NON-half-word boundary and
! both are followed by a CNOP that the page prints one half word
! further on:
!
!   line 13 at 216516.40, datum 14 blanks = 112 bits -> 216520.20,
!           and line 14 prints its CNOP at 216520.40.
!   line 51 at 216563.70, datum 10 blanks =  80 bits -> 216565.10,
!           and printed p.134 line 1 prints its CNOP at 216565.40.
!
! Both datum lengths were MEASURED off the page's character grid
! (ink-column runs at 400 dpi against a 39.9 px pitch), not fitted
! to the deltas: line 13's terminating X sits at character 25 with
! the comma at 10, line 51's at 21.  strap_asm's CNOP advances the
! same way, so both rows check; the agreement of two independent
! pages with the assembler is the point.
!
! THE OTHER FIVE ENTRY-MODE DATA MEASURE EXACTLY, with no CNOP to
! absorb an error -- each one's length is pinned by the NEXT row's
! printed LOCATION and the character grid gives the same number:
!
!   line 12  216513.00 -> 216516.40  = 224 bits = 28 chars
!   line 16  216521.10 -> 216523.00  = 120 bits = 15 chars
!   line 17  216523.00 -> 216530.00  = 320 bits = 40 chars
!   line 49  216555.00 -> 216562.20  = 336 bits = 42 chars
!   line 50  216562.20 -> 216563.70  = 104 bits = 13 chars
!
! >>> THE SPACES INSIDE THOSE DATA ARE DATA. <<<  In entry mode the
! blank after the comma is a character (docs/transcription_workflow
! .md, "In entry mode the space after the comma is DATA"), so the
! runs of blanks below are transcribed to the column and must not be
! tidied.  No !CHECK can test them -- MCP's listing prints NOTHING
! in the BINARY OUTPUT column for an (AX)DD or (IQSX)DD row -- but
! the LOCATION of the row after each one does, and those checks are
! declared.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS SETTLED, AND HOW
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ZSPLP9 (line 42).  The last glyph is a 9, read at 1200 dpi (closed
!   upper bowl, straight descender), and the volume OCR of this very
!   row agrees -- docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt line 6989 reads
!   "SIC,ZSPLP9".  Worth saying because the OCR renders the same
!   name "ZSPLPS" on three other pages.
! SDISP (line 47).  Five glyphs, read at 1200 dpi: S, D (straight
!   vertical left stem, bowl worn through), I, S, P.  NO embedded
!   blank on this page.  pp.99/119/120/122/124 print "S DISP";
!   STRAP ignores blanks in a name, so they are one symbol.  The
!   PRINTED form is used here.
! Three more names this page prints solid that other pages print
!   with a blank: SL (p.103 line 14 "S L"), STIC (p.128 "S TIC"),
!   SYCOCH (p.103 "S YCOCH").  Printed forms used; alternates named.
! tests/check_symbol_spellings.py, run over the landed decks plus
!   this one, reports "1153 symbol definitions, no symbol spelled two
!   ways".  Eleven of this page's names group with a landed deck at
!   the same bit: SL, SYCOCH, STMMI, YSFIC, STIC, YFXTS, YEXEFX,
!   YMSF, STLR, SLRBU, YMISCO, SDISP.  YFXTS/YEXEFX/YMSF are the
!   strongest of these, because they are symbols this page DEFINES
!   and printed p.114 referenced them before this page was read.
! "CO" vs "00" in the byte column.  Lines 18 and 19 are the SAME
!   instruction, "B,WRAM"; line 18's byte prints open and line 19's
!   closed, and both are 00.  Line 32's byte really is C0 -- printed
!   p.128 line 1 prints the same mnemonic BZRZ with a clean C0.  The
!   discriminator is what PRODUCED the byte, not the row's ink.
! Line 41's "FC" is F0: printed p.18 prints CM1111(BU,1) six times
!   and every one is "001000.36 F0" (docs/transcription_workflow.md).
! Line 30's "C2" is 02: printed p.128 line 7's LCI prints 02.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SEVEN PRINTED FORMS TESTED BEFORE THEY WERE WRITTEN; ALL SEVEN
! ASSEMBLE AS PRINTED.  No substitution anywhere in this deck.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   L (BU,1),STIC+.18,2          blank between the op and the "("
!   CW(CCR),YMFCF,3,YMCPC2       CCR as a CW modifier (= flags 0o100)
!   TI,16,STLR,SLRBU             and TI,14,...  -- the T family
!   (AX)DD(BU),-   ...           a datum that STARTS with "-"
!   CCW,0($1),YUXSAV             three-field I/O with an indexed first
!                                operand
!   ,YMIMIN  and  ,8.0           A STATEMENT WITH A BLANK OPERATION
!                                FIELD, lines 44-45.  Not in the
!                                accepted-forms list any brief has
!                                carried, and strap_asm needs no
!                                change: it emits "aaaaaa.oo 80", the
!                                parameter half words of the
!                                SIC/B calling sequence at lines
!                                42-45, exactly as printed.
!
! THE COUNT FIELD OF TI IS CHECKED, not coincidence.  Line 20's
! "TI,16" prints its second half word ".00" and line 21's "TI,14"
! prints ".34".  Measured by varying the count alone: 16 -> .00,
! 14 -> .34, 12 -> .30, with the address bits unchanged.  So the
! page's two rows pin the count field twice.
!
! YPPEM / YPEIC / YMIMIN / YMIMIC are confirmed by their own data,
!   which is English: "INTERRUPT AT LOCATION", "INTERRUPT-...
!   INSTRUCTION COUNTER", "CONTENTS".  YMISCO is confirmed by the
!   comment column, "-GET CURRENT MASKABLE INTERRUPT / -COUNT.", and
!   by its defining card (below).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS.  WHAT IS OBSERVED AND WHAT IS CONVENTION
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FULLY OBSERVED -- these come off a VFL instruction's ADDRESS half
! word, where all 24 bits print, so the bit offset is read:
!
!   SL      215001.04   p.103 line 14 "S L SYN(BU,1),S COM RG+0.04".
!                       Line 41's CM1111 prints 215001.04 80.
!   YMFCF   216425.00   line 3/5 print 216426.00 for "YMFCF+1.0" and
!                       line 11's CW prints 216425.00 for YMFCF
!                       itself.  The defining card is on printed
!                       p.131: OCR line 6870, "216425.CC * ... YMFCF
!                       DR(IN),(3)" -- a three-word reservation,
!                       which is why line 11 writes a count of 3.
!   YUXSAV  231363.00   line 6 prints 231363.21 and line 7 prints
!                       231363.30 for "YUXSAV+.24" (0o30 = 24).  OCR
!                       line 7039 carries "231363.C0+ ... YSFLCR
!                       SYN YUXSAV", a second name for the cell.
!   YSFIC   216604.00   line 4's LF prints 216604.00.  LANDED:
!                       decks/mcp_bootstrap_p110.strap line 193.
!   STIC    215265.00   lines 26/28.  LANDED by p110/111/112/118.
!   STLR    215230.00   line 20.  LANDED by p117/p118; p.117 line 12
!                       is the defining card.
!   SLRBU   215324.00   line 20.  LANDED by p116/p117.
!   YSFBCR  215224.00   line 24's LX prints 215224.02.  OCR line
!                       7038 is the defining card: "215224.0C+ ...
!                       YSFBCR SYN,S BNDRS".  So YSFBCR and S BNDRS
!                       (pp.116/117/124) are TWO DELIBERATE NAMES for
!                       one cell, like p.99's S UN A / S UN A A --
!                       not a misreading of either.
!   YMISCO  215466.40   lines 37/39 print 215466.42 and 215466.43 --
!                       bit 18 (0o40) set in BOTH, so the half word
!                       is read, and the low bits are the LC/SC
!                       operation difference.  LANDED: decks/
!                       mcp_bootstrap_p116.strap line 291, "YMISCO
!                       CF,50" at 215466.40, "-MASKABLE INTERRUPT
!                       COUNTER", which is this page's own comment.
!
! PINNED ONLY TO THE HALF WORD -- these come off a branch, an LVI or
! an index instruction, whose printed ".oo" field holds bits 18-23
! of which only bit 18 is address.  Writing ".0" is a CONVENTION and
! no !CHECK here can test the bits below it (docs/transcription_
! workflow.md, "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE", item 1):
!
!   SYCOCH  215006.00   line 1 prints 215006.02 (reg $1, bit 18 = 0).
!                       LANDED: p.103 line 37 "S YCOCH VF,(8)23.40"
!                       at 215006.00, "-CONSOLE CHANNEL NUMBER".
!   WRAM    217343.00   lines 18/19 print 217343.10.  OCR line 7591
!                       is the defining card at 217343.00.
!   SDISP   217372.00   line 47 prints 217372.10.  LANDED by the
!                       p117/p119/p120/p124 decks.
!   STMMI   000403.00   line 46 prints 000403.35 01 (LVI, reg $14).
!                       LANDED: decks/mcp_bootstrap_p107.strap line
!                       269, "STMMI SYN,(16)0103.0" -- 0x103 = 0o403
!                       -- "-13 50 MASKABLE INTERRUPTS".
!   ZSPLP9  224052.00   line 42 prints 224052.00 80.
!   ZSPLPR  224046.40   line 43 prints 224046.50 00; B's operation
!                       bits are .10, so the extra 0o40 IS bit 18
!                       and the HALF WORD is read -- .40, not .00.
!
SYCOCH  SYN, (8)215006.0
SL      SYN(BU,1), (8)215001.04
STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0
SLRBU   SYN, (8)215324.0
YSFBCR  SYN, (8)215224.0
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0
YMISCO  SYN, (8)215466.40
YMFCF   SYN, (8)216425.0
YSFIC   SYN, (8)216604.0
WRAM    SYN, (8)217343.0
SDISP   SYN, (8)217372.0
ZSPLPR  SYN, (8)224046.40
ZSPLP9  SYN, (8)224052.0
STMMI   SYN, (8)403.0
YUXSAV  SYN, (8)231363.0
!
        SLC, (8)216500.40
!
YMCPPE  LV, $1, SYCOCH                 ! line  1 -GET ABSOLUTE ADDRESSES FOR
        REL(SEOP), 0($1)               ! line  2 -CLEAR BOTH CHANNELS.
        CM1111(BU,64), YMFCF+1.0       ! line  3
        LF(BU,21,3), YSFIC             ! line  4 -SET UP INT. ADDRESS FOR
        SF(BU,28,4), YMFCF+1.0         ! line  5 -CONSOLE LIGHTS.
        CCW, 0($1), YUXSAV             ! line  6
        BB, YUXSAV+.24, $-1.0          ! line  7
        W(SEOP), 0($1), YMCPCW         ! line  8
YMCPHP  BD, YMCPHP                     ! line  9
YMCPC2  CW, YMCPCM, 7, 0               ! line 10
YMCPCW  CW(CCR), YMFCF, 3, YMCPC2      ! line 11
YPPEM   (AX)DD(BU),-     INTERRUPT AT LOCATION X
YPEIC   (AX)DD(BU),              X
        CNOP                           ! line 14
YMCPCM  DD(BU,8), (2)11111101          ! line 15
        (IQSX)DD(BU),MCP ERROR-...  X
YMCPIN  (IQSX)DD(BU),      INTERRUPT AT ABOVE LOCATION.      X
YFXTS   B, WRAM                        ! line 18
YEXEFX  B, WRAM                        ! line 19
YMSF    TI, 16, STLR, SLRBU            ! line 20
        TI, 14, STLR+16., SLRBU+16.    ! line 21
        L(BU,32), 0($1)                ! line 22 -LOAD IDENTIFYING INITIALS-...
        ST(BU,32), YMIMIN+.16          ! line 23 -STORE IN SPOOL MESSAGE.
        LX, $1, YSFBCR                 ! line 24 -SET NEW BOUNDARY CONTROL
        SX, $1, 3.0                    ! line 25
        L (BU,1), STIC+.18, 2          ! line 26 -CONVERT IC TO BCD.
        LFI(BU,8), (2)00111011, 8      ! line 27
        LF(BU,18,3), STIC, 16          ! line 28
        LVI, $1, 0                     ! line 29
        LCI, $1, 8                     ! line 30
YSFCL1  CT0101(BU,8), 0, 0($1)         ! line 31
        BZRZ, $+1.32                   ! line 32
        LFI(BU,8), (2)00001010, 0($1)  ! line 33
        V+I, $1, 4.0                   ! line 34
        CB, $1, YSFCL1                 ! line 35
        ST(BU), YMIMIC                 ! line 36
        LC, $1, YMISCO                 ! line 37 -GET CURRENT MASKABLE INTERRUPT
        C-I, $1, 1.0                   ! line 38 -COUNT. IF COUNT REACHES ZERO, P.P. IS
        SC, $1, YMISCO                 ! line 39 -TO BE KICKED OFF THE MACHINE
        BXCZ, YTMMI                    ! line 40
        CM1111(BU,1), SL               ! line 41
        SIC, ZSPLP9                    ! line 42
        B, ZSPLPR                      ! line 43
        , YMIMIN                       ! line 44
        , 8.0                          ! line 45
YTMMI   LVI, $14, STMMI                ! line 46
        B, SDISP                       ! line 47
        CNOP                           ! line 48
YMIMIN  (AX)DD(BU),-       INTERRUPT-... INSTRUCTION COUNTER X
        (AX)DD(BU),CONTENTS  -  X
YMIMIC  (AX)DD(BU),          X
        END
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, for listing_oracle
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!SYM   YMCPPE   216500.40
!SYM   YMCPHP   216510.00
!SYM   YMCPC2   216511.00
!SYM   YMCPCW   216512.00
!SYM   YPPEM    216513.00
!SYM   YPEIC    216516.40
!SYM   YMCPCM   216521.00
!SYM   YMCPIN   216523.00
!SYM   YFXTS    216530.00
!SYM   YEXEFX   216530.40
!SYM   YMSF     216531.00
!SYM   YSFCL1   216542.00
!SYM   YTMMI    216553.40
!SYM   YMIMIN   216555.00
!SYM   YMIMIC   216563.70
!
!CHECK 216500.40 | 215006.02 30 | line  1 YMCPPE LV,$1,SYCOCH
!CHECK 216501.00 | 000000.00 81 000000.33 00 | line  2 REL(SEOP),0($1)
!CHECK 216502.00 | 216426.00 80 000000.36 F0 | line  3 CM1111(BU,64),YMFCF+1.0
!CHECK 216503.00 | 216604.00 80 025300.06 70 | line  4 LF(BU,21,3),YSFIC
!CHECK 216504.00 | 216426.00 80 034400.12 F0 | line  5 SF(BU,28,4),YMFCF+1.0
!CHECK 216505.00 | 000000.00 81 231363.21 00 | line  6 CCW,0($1),YUXSAV
!CHECK 216506.00 | 231363.30 80 216505.34 02 | line  7 BB,YUXSAV+.24,$-1.0
!CHECK 216507.00 | 000000.00 81 216512.13 00 | line  8 W(SEOP),0($1),YMCPCW
!CHECK 216510.00 | 216510.04 00 | line  9 YMCPHP BD,YMCPHP
!CHECK 216511.00 | 216521.00+ 000 000007 000000 | line 10 YMCPC2 CW,YMCPCM,7,0
!CHECK 216512.00 | 216425.00+ 100 000003 216511 | line 11 YMCPCW CW(CCR),YMFCF,3,YMCPC2
!CHECK 216520.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 14 CNOP -- its LOCATION is the check on line 13's 14-blank datum
!CHECK 216521.00 | 375 | line 15 YMCPCM DD(BU,8),(2)11111101 | 8
!CHECK 216530.00 | 217343.10 00 | line 18 YFXTS B,WRAM -- its LOCATION is the check on line 17's 40-char datum
!CHECK 216530.40 | 217343.10 00 | line 19 YEXEFX B,WRAM
!CHECK 216531.00 | 215230.00 80 215324.00 A0 | line 20 YMSF TI,16,STLR,SLRBU
!CHECK 216532.00 | 215250.00 80 215344.34 A0 | line 21 TI,14,STLR+16.,SLRBU+16.
!CHECK 216533.00 | 000000.00 81 040000.20 50 | line 22 L(BU,32),0($1)
!CHECK 216534.00 | 216555.20 80 040000.20 D0 | line 23 ST(BU,32),YMIMIN+.16
!CHECK 216535.00 | 215224.02 10 | line 24 LX,$1,YSFBCR
!CHECK 216535.40 | 000003.03 10 | line 25 SX,$1,3.0
!CHECK 216536.00 | 215265.22 80 001001.20 50 | line 26 L (BU,1),STIC+.18,2
!CHECK 216537.00 | 166000.00 80 410004.06 70 | line 27 LFI(BU,8),(2)00111011,8
!CHECK 216540.00 | 215265.00 80 022310.06 70 | line 28 LF(BU,18,3),STIC,16
!CHECK 216541.00 | 000000.03 01 | line 29 LVI,$1,0
!CHECK 216541.40 | 000010.03 02 | line 30 LCI,$1,8
!CHECK 216542.00 | 000000.00 80 010000.13 71 | line 31 YSFCL1 CT0101(BU,8),0,0($1)
!CHECK 216543.00 | 216544.74 C0 | line 32 BZRZ,$+1.32
!CHECK 216543.40 | 024000.00 80 410000.06 71 | line 33 LFI(BU,8),(2)00001010,0($1)
!CHECK 216544.40 | 000004.03 05 | line 34 V+I,$1,4.0
!CHECK 216545.00 | 216542.02 48 | line 35 CB,$1,YSFCL1
!CHECK 216545.40 | 216563.70 80 000000.20 D0 | line 36 ST(BU),YMIMIC
!CHECK 216546.40 | 215466.42 50 | line 37 LC,$1,YMISCO
!CHECK 216547.00 | 000001.03 08 | line 38 C-I,$1,1.0
!CHECK 216547.40 | 215466.43 50 | line 39 SC,$1,YMISCO
!CHECK 216550.00 | 216553.70 42 | line 40 BXCZ,YTMMI
!CHECK 216550.40 | 215001.04 80 001000.36 F0 | line 41 CM1111(BU,1),SL
!CHECK 216551.40 | 224052.00 80 | line 42 SIC,ZSPLP9
!CHECK 216552.00 | 224046.50 00 | line 43 B,ZSPLPR
!CHECK 216552.40 | 216555.00 80 | line 44 ,YMIMIN -- blank operation, printed as a bare ",YMIMIN"
!CHECK 216553.00 | 000010.00 80 | line 45 ,8.0
!CHECK 216553.40 | 000403.35 01 | line 46 YTMMI LVI,$14,STMMI
!CHECK 216554.00 | 217372.10 00 | line 47 B,SDISP
!CHECK 216554.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 48 CNOP
